  "behavior": "Freeze the database-generated journal generation in preparation, every phase update, execution and acknowledgement. Shared core recovery rejects a different generation after a lost reply. Native and browser adapters reject queued replacements before mutation; UI recovery, publication and folder grant rechecks retain the original identity.",
  "implementation": "Shared core transaction orchestration, owned storage CAS and the existing workspace transaction facade; browser/native transports supply filesystem, locking and persistence primitives. Generation is immutable record identity, not an execution lease.",
